# XSH close()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# XSH.close.002 relies on the lowest-descriptor rule, hence "uses" in
# MODULE: if that rule fails, these results would mean nothing.

assertion  XSH.close.001
anchor     functions/close.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       close() of an open regular-file descriptor, with no signal and
           no I/O error, returns 0.
test       t/001-returns-zero.c

assertion  XSH.close.002
anchor     functions/close.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       A closed descriptor is available again: the next open() returns
           that same number.
test       t/002-reused.c

assertion  XSH.close.003
anchor     functions/close.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       After close(), the descriptor is no longer open (fcntl F_GETFD
           fails with EBADF).
test       t/003-deallocated.c

assertion  XSH.close.004
anchor     functions/close.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      1988
says       close() of a descriptor that is not open returns -1 with EBADF.
test       t/004-ebadf.c
